{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE PAGE SHELL — Phase 1 of design_handoff_africa_gates
  snippets/twig/page-shell.twig, adapted to this repo · REFERENCE §6.7
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The root is 100dvh and does not scroll; `<main class="ag-main">` is the only
  scroller, so every bar is a plain flex child that cannot move with the content.
  A page the redesign rebuilds extends THIS layout. `layout/gates.twig` keeps
  serving every page no phase has reached, and the two never nest: a shell inside a
  layout whose body scrolls is a one-viewport window onto a document that carries
  on underneath it.

  ── WHERE THIS DIFFERS FROM THE SNIPPET, AND WHY ─────────────────────────────

  · `<html class="ag-shelled">` arms the overflow lock, which is scoped to this
    layout rather than global — deviation #1, see shell.css and PHASE-1.md.
  · `lang` and `dir` are `lang()` / `lang_dir()`, the one answer LanguageMiddleware
    settles per request from `?lang=` and the `ag_lang` cookie. The snippet's
    `lang == 'ar'` test would be a second resolver for the same value.
  · The head script is `partials/a11y-head.twig` (nonced, before any stylesheet), not
    `source('snippets/a11y-head.js')` — the repo's store and the snippet's differ.
  · Colour is not a stylesheet. Every colour and shadow token comes from
    Support\Accent through `ag_accents()`, in a nonced <style> BEFORE the links, the
    same block every layout writes (GAPS §8 Q1).
  · The snippet includes `partials/nav.twig` and `partials/gee.twig`. Neither
    exists: the site header is `partials/site-header.twig`, which a page puts in
    `header`, and Gee on this layout is GAPS §8 Q19, unanswered — so `gee` stays an
    empty block rather than this phase inventing Phase 2's or Phase 3's partials.
  · `components/chrome.css` and `components/library.css` load right after
    `components.css`: they are other phases' rules carved OUT of it, in the
    position they held inside it (GAPS §7.2).

  ── BLOCKS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    a11y_head     Display & reading, before first paint
    head_styles   page-local stylesheet links or a nonced <style>
    header        SiteHeader, tablet and desktop                    (Phase 2)
    app_bar       the phone AppBar, root or child                    (Phase 2)
    content       inside <main> — the ONLY scroller
    bottom_bar    an action bar OR a tab bar, each [data-bottom-ui]  (Phase 2)
    gee           empty until Q19                                    (Phase 3)
    sheets        Menu and Quick settings, shell-level              (Phase 2)
    foot_scripts  page-local scripts, nonced
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ lang() }}" dir="{{ lang_dir() }}" class="ag-shelled">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  {# `viewport-fit=cover`, or every `env(safe-area-inset-*)` resolves to zero. #}
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title>{{ page_title|default('Africa GATES') }}</title>
  {% if meta_description is defined %}<meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description }}">{% endif %}
  {% if meta_robots is defined %}<meta name="robots" content="{{ meta_robots }}">{% endif %}

  {# Before any stylesheet: a linked script runs after first paint, and somebody who
     asked for 150% text would watch the page draw at 100% and jump. #}
  {% block a11y_head %}{% include 'partials/a11y-head.twig' %}{% endblock %}

  {# §6.2: Playfair Display 700, DM Sans 400–700, JetBrains Mono 500/700, swap. #}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Playfair+Display:wght@700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@500;700&display=swap">

  <style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">{{ ag_accents()|raw }}</style>

  {# In cascade order: the tokens, the shell, the base components, the rules carved
     out of them, then the form states that refine `.ag-field`. #}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/tokens.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/shell.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/chrome.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/library.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/forms.css') }}">
  {% block head_styles %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body data-page="{{ page_id|default('') }}">
  <a class="ag-skip" href="#main">{{ 'Skip to content'|trans }}</a>

  <div class="ag-shell">
    {% block header %}{% endblock %}
    {% block app_bar %}{% endblock %}

    <main class="ag-main" id="main">
      {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    </main>

    {% block bottom_bar %}{% endblock %}
  </div>

  {% block gee %}{% endblock %}

  {# The Menu is reachable from the tab bar on every phone page and Quick settings
     from every root app bar, so they belong to the shell, not to each page — a
     partial every page must remember is a partial the next page forgets. Both
     start `inert`. #}
  {% block sheets %}
    {% include 'partials/menu-sheet.twig' %}
    {% include 'partials/quick-settings.twig' %}
  {% endblock %}

  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/shell.js') }}"></script>
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/a11y.js') }}"></script>
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/chrome.js') }}"></script>
  {# The shared validator: a form here that says `novalidate data-ag-validate` has
     turned the browser's own messages off on the promise this replaces them. #}
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/form-validate.js') }}"></script>
  {% block foot_scripts %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
